From 1f4dbbd5c7ab511943bba0956a9ac031b716d5a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: starbite <starbite@local>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 17:56:59 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] patch: 0309-port-critical-exit-log.patch

port: diagnostics for launchd dying early. proc_handle_critical_exit()
panics for pid 1 before proc_prepareexit() reaches the SWEET crash log
(0043/0044), and within ~30 s of boot, before the persistent log's first
10 s flush. For the critical process it now prints the crash log (pc, lr,
user backtrace, strings for SIGABRT) and flushes the console ring to the
flash log synchronously (herolte_log_flush_now, HEROLTE boards) before
the core dump and panic. herolte_log_thread's body moved to
herolte_log_write(), shared by both.

build: sweettracename=<p_comm> traces a process by name; its failing syscalls are always logged with the path argument

build: sweetmsg=1 dumps the printable text of the traced process's Mach messages (XPC replies)

build: sweetmsg follows OOL descriptors and prints a hex header for text-less messages

build: failing Mach traps of the traced process are always logged

build: persona(494) syscalls are logged from every process

build: sweetreboot=N: the log thread flushes and resets into recovery after N seconds

build: persona syscalls are only logged for the traced process again

build: sweetdumpfile=<path>: the tail of that file is printed to the console before the sweetreboot reset

build: sweetreboot also resets on a panic, after copying the panic log tail to the ramoops pmsg ring (armed at STARTUP KMEM)
